The Arbiter has five states. The priority order of bits in each state is given as follows-
Initial - 0 > 1 > 2 > 3
S1 - 1 > 2 > 3 > 0
S2 - 2 > 3 > 0 > 1
S3 - 3 > 0 > 1 > 2
S4 - 0 > 1 > 2 > 3
It might appear that initial and S4 are redundant but they have different outputs. 

I tried a Moore approach, I don't know about the Mealy version of this.

So at each state, req variable is checked and according to the priority next state is assigned as well as the output.
    
